  "workoutHelp": "Explain",
  "helpTitle": "Effort and set types",
  "helpEffortTitle": "Effort",
  "helpEffortBody": "Right after you tick a set, the app asks how hard it was: under the rest countdown while you rest, or in place of the next set when no rest starts. It's optional: it goes away with the rest, or skip it. To answer later or change it, select the done set. Warm-ups aren't rated. The app saves it with the set and shows it in your workout history, so you can look back at how hard you trained.",
  "helpScaleFeel": "By feel: how many more reps you could have done with good form.",
  "helpScaleRir": "Reps in reserve (RIR): how many more reps you could have done with good form.",
  "helpScaleRpe": "Rate of perceived exertion (RPE): 10 means you had nothing left; each point lower is one more rep you could have done.",
